\ Resolving a type annotation runs the named parse-time word. A word that throws there is
\ dropped so the caller can report its own diagnostic, and the drop must be complete: the
\ error reported next renders only its own chain. Before the shield, the dropped throw left
\ a pending frame that rendered as the innermost row, moving the word name, the location,
\ and the stack effect onto the annotation word's body.
\
\ The pin goes through `native.parse-stack-effect` because an annotation that fails to
\ resolve in source aborts the parse, and a parse diagnostic renders no chain rows. The
\ runtime entry point shares the same parser and turns the failure into an ordinary error,
\ so the render is reached with the residue still live. No flags, so the interpreted and
\ eager suites bind one golden.

annot-boom: parse-time [ 1 0 / ] ;

"n: annot-boom -- " native.parse-stack-effect
